cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  InterSubMod is currently a non-clinical, non-production research handoff
  snapshot, not a release-ready clinical or lineage-calling product. Cite the
  exact immutable commit you used. No DOI, versioned release, or verified
  individual author list is assigned yet. A GPL-3.0 license text is present,
  but the project-level SPDX choice still requires maintainer confirmation.
title: InterSubMod
type: software
authors:
  - name: InterSubMod contributors
abstract: >-
  InterSubMod computes per-region methylation, distance, read clustering, and
  statistics from phased Oxford Nanopore research inputs. Exact-PS candidate
  reconstruction and LongLineage are separate, versioned provenance chains;
  they are not functions of the inter_sub_mod executable. The frozen
  2026-08-01 authority supports zero confirmed cellular subclones and zero
  confirmed linear ancestry relationships. Methylation is association-only.
  Allele-specific copy number, copy-neutral LOH, purity, and multiplicity are
  not integrated into the frozen candidate reconstruction; optional --loh-bed
  input is stratification/annotation only and does not produce CN/LOH-corrected
  cellular inference. The 88.2579 percent value is a model-conditional
  graph-shape statistic, not biological accuracy or prevalence. LongLineage
  remains a non-production research-preview candidate with P3/P4/P5/P7/P8
  BLOCKED.
repository-code: https://github.com/liaoyoyo/InterSubMod
url: https://github.com/liaoyoyo/InterSubMod
keywords:
  - Oxford Nanopore sequencing
  - somatic variant co-occurrence
  - methylation association
  - candidate mutation-state reconstruction
  - research handoff
